shape theory.operations : theory.forcing, theory.branching.canopy {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Section 14 (Structural Operations).
//
// Theorem 14.1 (Forcing Shapes Are Catalytic): a forcing shape
// accelerates resolution without altering which outcomes are
// coherent. Not consumed. "Forcing" and "catalysis" are the same
// structural action from two perspectives.
//
// Definition 14.2 (Controlled Resolution): deliberate management
// of what comes into contact, in what order, at what rate.
// Not coercion: manages sequence and rate without suppressing
// structural possibilities.
//
// Definition 14.4 (Canopy Gap): the set of asymmetries present in
// an emergent canopy but absent from a constructed projection.
//
// Theorem 14.5 (Convergence Criterion): a projection fully models
// a system iff their canopies match (gap is empty).
//
// Corollary 14.6 (Progressive Understanding): each identified
// asymmetry strictly reduces the canopy gap. Understanding is
// progressive and measurable.
//
// Derives from: theory.forcing, theory.branching.canopy
  """
}
